If the three addresses are one person, review requests for the old `alt-three.com` address should go to the active one. Graham Campbell then holds 84.8% of the lines. Under the merged count, the bus factor is 1 at both the 50% and 80% thresholds. That bus factor counts surviving lines. It does not measure who understands the code. Unmerged, the bus factor is 1 at 50% and 2 at 80%.

**What was left out or adjusted**
- **Excluded bot:** StyleCI Bot, 11 lines and 1 commit. Its lines are not credited to anyone.
- **Mechanical rewrites:** I checked 47 commits holding surviving lines and set aside none, so the figures include every commit.
- **Copy detection:** the figures use `-w -M -C`. Without copy detection, Graham Campbell would hold 85.8% (718 lines) merged, instead of 84.8%. Vance Lucas would drop from 8 lines to 0.
- **Moved code:** 418 of 848 lines (49.3%) were written in other paths and moved or copied into `src/Parser`. The largest sources are `src/Parser.php`, `src/Regex/Regex.php` and `src/Lines.php`. The credit goes to the authors of those lines, not to whoever moved them.

**Limits of these numbers:** they don't show code quality, review work, design done outside the code, or code that was deleted on purpose. Surviving lines show whose code is still here. They don't show who is the best reviewer.
